-{"status": "in_progress", "id": "AUG-209", "title": "Live DuckBrain arm aborts 72 tests at setup with 503 SERIALIZER_LOCKED instead of classifying concurrent-writer contention, so the full gate reds and board commits need a bypass", "detail": {"fingerprint": "434e3bf41a2b019716f8436cd936e8b716e2327901f562d3393c4277409e1c39"}, "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "Filed by the COS auger card manager 2026-11-24T21:00Z from a measured gate run on an otherwise untouched tree: the staged diff was two board JSONL lines (one added task row, one added event row). Guard log .gitreins/logs/guard-20261124T204154.877674Z.log records '804 passed, 2 skipped, 72 errors in 1920.09s', overall FAIL, first_failing_test reported as tests/test_auger.py::test_feedback_stamps_no_gate_check_when_no_evidence_could_answer. Root cause is a single one: the decided fixture in tests/conftest.py:1042 calls answer() which reaches auger.py cmd_answer insert() and the store answers 503 with code SERIALIZER_LOCKED, 'Namespace auger-pytest-a6a09647-8e35cf4548bc is locked by another writer process'; insert() raises SystemExit, so 71 further tests ERROR at setup and the single 503 cascades into a battery-wide red. The log carries exactly 1 SERIALIZER_LOCKED line and 71 downstream AssertionError lines, i.e. one environment fault presented as 72 failures. This is the same contention family AUG-197 (complete) was supposed to contain for the teardown 409 'Push in flight' arm, reproduced here on the INSERT path at setup, so AUG-197's classification does not cover this arm. Consequence paid today: the board commit for AUG-208 could not land through the guarded path on a diff that touches no code, and the run had to be landed with a disclosed hook bypass (matching the repo's own precedent in docs/dogfood/2026-10-23-released-artifact-consumer-integration.md for docs/board-only diffs on a host whose gate hangs). Do NOT fix by weakening the assertions or by making 503 universally non-fatal: a lock held by a foreign writer is environment contention and must be a typed skip naming the contender, while every other 503 must still fail loudly. Related: AUG-197 (teardown 409 arm), AUG-208 (missing DUCKBRAIN_URL arm), AUG-194 (board shrink guard).", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-11-24T20:54:39Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-25T10:46:46Z", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": ["gate", "tests", "duckbrain", "concurrency"], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/auger-AUG-209", "branch": "wt/AUG-209", "sessions": ["foreman-20261125-1024"], "type": null, "worker_summary": null, "completed_at": null, "acceptance_criteria": "AC1 REPRODUCE: `bash tests/gate.sh` in full mode on this host with a concurrent writer holding the store ends with an ERROR-at-setup block whose first entry is the decided fixture and whose cause line reads 503 with code SERIALIZER_LOCKED, and the pytest tail reports the error count; paste the run's pytest tail and the cause line verbatim.\n\nAC2 CLASSIFY: a live write that receives status 503 carrying the code SERIALIZER_LOCKED is classified as environment contention - a typed skip that names the competing writer or namespace - instead of raising SystemExit from insert() and aborting every fixture-dependent test; prove it by holding the store's writer lock deliberately and running the affected subset, then quote the skip line and expect zero ERROR-at-setup entries.\n\nAC3 FAIL-CLOSED KEPT: a 503 that is NOT a lock (authentication, validation, or an unknown code) still fails loudly and is never downgraded to a skip; a committed test asserts that mapping and is red-proven against the pre-fix code.\n\nAC4 GATE MEANINGFUL: with no competing writer, `bash tests/gate.sh` in full mode ends GATE PASS and the same test count still runs, so the classification cannot turn the arm vacuously green; quote the passing tail and the count.\n\nAC5 COUNTED HONESTLY: the pytest summary no longer collapses one environment fault into a battery-wide error count - after the fix the summary attributes the skipped tests to the lock and leaves every genuine failure as a failure; expect the summary line quoted in the closing evidence.\n\nGATE ARM (COS card manager 2026-11-24): Run `grep -c SERIALIZER_LOCKED .gitreins/logs/guard-20261124T204154.877674Z.log`; expect the output 1, and Run `bash tests/gate.sh`; expect the pytest tail to attribute any lock-skipped tests to the competing writer.\n"}
